{
  "dom_id": "step-q174092",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14153326/assets/72f5c8ef7e4ee3beb67bb8ebdbe573da7718161cd4378064d160bbfc10affbee.png)\n\nUse the model above to compute the following result. Express your answer as a fraction in its lowest terms.\n\n$\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{5}{7}=$  \n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14153326/assets/f566a58700fa3c0671e4d1ebdd7609a7691ed7a269991be47344ce8afcebeac8.png)\n\nWe can break down our division problem as follows:\n\n- Computing $\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{5}{7}$ means we want to determine how many times $\\frac{5}{7}$ fits into $\\frac{3}{7}.$\n\n- Since both fractions have a *common denominator*, this is the *same* as determining how many times $5$ fits into $3.$\n\n- Therefore, instead of $\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{5}{7}$, we can simply compute $3÷5.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n3÷5=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{7}÷\\frac{5}{7}=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
